    "why": "0.10.0 (docs/plan-serif-joint-jags.md) cut serif brackets along the stroke's own edge, cut a leaning serif end level, cut the shallow stroke of a corner along its partner, and redrew the G and the italic r: the export and TTF digests of all five groups moved; tests/test_serif_joints.py::test_only_the_named_glyphs_changed_since_0_9_0 holds every other glyph outline, advance and kern to the 0.9.0 build. The darwin/26 entry was taken from the finished tree before its commit existed (--print) and is re-recorded under the --record guard at commit A; the other platforms are recorded by the record-baseline workflow from commit A. Before this the baseline was 0.7.0 at c5b4abb (earlier: 0.5.0 at 788760d)"
  }
